@*
   FILE ROLE: Demonstrates asset tag helpers (link, script, img with asp-append-version
              and asp-src-include/exclude), the environment tag helper, the partial
              tag helper, and the cache tag helper.

   SECTIONS IN THIS FILE:
     1. asp-append-version   — cache-busting on link, script, and img
     2. asp-src-include/exclude — glob-based script/style bundling
     3. environment tag helper  — conditional content by environment name
     4. partial tag helper      — rendering partial views with optional model
     5. cache tag helper        — output caching with expiry and vary-by options
*@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Asset Tag Helpers";
}

<h2>Asset Tag Helpers</h2>

@* ============================================================
   SECTION 1: asp-append-version — CACHE BUSTING
   <link asp-append-version="true" href="~/css/site.css" />
   <script asp-append-version="true" src="~/js/app.js"></script>
   <img asp-append-version="true" src="~/images/logo.png" />

   HOW IT WORKS:
     At runtime, IFileVersionProvider computes a SHA-256 hash of the file content
     and appends it as a query-string parameter: ?v=abc123...
     Example output:
       <link href="/css/site.css?v=s47rfh3Kmg..." rel="stylesheet" />
       <script src="/js/app.js?v=XY29as7..." ></script>
       <img src="/images/logo.png?v=Qp8..." alt="Logo" />

   WHY IT MATTERS:
     Browsers cache static files aggressively.  Without a version token, users
     may receive a stale .css or .js after a deployment.
     ?v=hash forces a new download every time the file CONTENT changes,
     but keeps the cache hit when the file is unchanged between requests.

   REQUIREMENTS:
     - app.UseStaticFiles() must be in the pipeline (Program.cs) ← already done
     - The file must exist in wwwroot/ at runtime (not required for dotnet build)
     - IFileVersionProvider is registered by AddControllersWithViews()

   NOTE: For this tutorial's build these files do not exist in wwwroot/ —
         the tag helper silently omits the ?v= suffix when the file is absent.
   ============================================================ *@
<h4>1. asp-append-version</h4>

<link rel="stylesheet" asp-append-version="true" href="~/css/site.css" />
@* Renders: <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/site.css?v=SHA256hash" /> *@

<script asp-append-version="true" src="~/js/app.js"></script>
@* Renders: <script src="/js/app.js?v=SHA256hash"></script> *@

<img asp-append-version="true" src="~/images/logo.png" alt="Logo" class="img-fluid" />
@* Renders: <img src="/images/logo.png?v=SHA256hash" alt="Logo" class="img-fluid" /> *@

@* ============================================================
   SECTION 2: asp-src-include / asp-src-exclude — GLOB BUNDLING
   <link asp-src-include="~/css/**\/*.css" rel="stylesheet" />
   <script asp-src-include="~/js/**\/*.js" asp-src-exclude="~/js/vendor.js"></script>

   asp-src-include uses Microsoft.Extensions.FileSystemGlobbing patterns:
     **\/*.css    → all .css files in any subdirectory of ~/css/
     ~/js/*.js   → all .js files directly in ~/js/ (no subdirs)

   asp-src-exclude filters OUT files that match the pattern.
   Both attributes accept comma-separated patterns.

   Result: ONE <link> or <script> element is emitted PER matched file.
   This is NOT a bundler — use it for development convenience or small projects.
   For production, use a real bundler (e.g. WebOptimizer, esbuild, webpack).

   asp-append-version can be combined with asp-src-include.
   ============================================================ *@
<h4>2. asp-src-include / asp-src-exclude</h4>

@* Renders one <link> per .css file found in wwwroot/css/ (all subdirs) *@
<link asp-src-include="~/css/**/*.css" rel="stylesheet" />

@* Renders one <script> per .js file in wwwroot/js/, excluding vendor.js *@
<script asp-src-include="~/js/**/*.js" asp-src-exclude="~/js/vendor.js"></script>

@* ============================================================
   SECTION 3: ENVIRONMENT TAG HELPER
   <environment include="...">...</environment>
   <environment exclude="...">...</environment>

   Renders its content only when the hosting environment name matches.
   Environment name is set by ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT env variable:
     Development | Staging | Production  (case-insensitive comparison)

   include="env1,env2"  → renders if current env is IN the comma-separated list
   exclude="env1,env2"  → renders if current env is NOT in the list

   Common use: serve non-minified assets in Development, minified in Production.

   The <environment> element itself is NOT emitted in the HTML output.
   Only its CONTENTS appear (or not) depending on the environment.
   ============================================================ *@
<h4>3. Environment Tag Helper</h4>

<environment include="Development">
    @* Renders ONLY in the Development environment *@
    <p class="text-warning">
        <strong>Dev mode:</strong> verbose logging and non-minified assets active.
    </p>
    @* Serve unminified CSS in dev — easier to debug *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/site.css" />
    <script src="~/js/app.js"></script>
</environment>

<environment exclude="Development">
    @* Renders in Staging and Production (any env that is NOT Development) *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" asp-append-version="true" href="~/css/site.min.css" />
    <script asp-append-version="true" src="~/js/app.min.js"></script>
</environment>

@* ============================================================
   SECTION 4: PARTIAL TAG HELPER
   <partial name="ViewName" />
   <partial name="ViewName" model="@someObject" />

   Renders a partial view synchronously (or asynchronously — the runtime picks).
   Name resolution follows standard Razor view search order.

   Attribute    | Purpose
   -------------|----------------------------------------------------------
   name         | Partial view name or path ("_MyPartial" or "~/Views/...")
   model        | Strongly-typed model passed to the partial (optional)
   for          | Model expression — binds a property of the parent model
   view-data    | ViewDataDictionary passed to the partial (rare)

   Comparison: Html.Partial vs <partial> tag helper
     @Html.Partial("_Name")               → synchronous (deprecated for async scenarios)
     @await Html.PartialAsync("_Name")    → async, explicit
     <partial name="_Name" />             → recommended; async under the hood

   The example below renders _ContactInfo.cshtml from Views/Shared/.
   ============================================================ *@
<h4>4. Partial Tag Helper</h4>

@* No-model partial — partial uses the parent's ViewData *@
<partial name="_ContactInfo" />

@* Partial with an explicit model object (parent model or a sub-property) *@
@* <partial name="_AddressCard" model="@Model.ShippingAddress" /> *@

@* ============================================================
   SECTION 5: CACHE TAG HELPER
   <cache expires-after="@TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5)"
          vary-by-user="true"
          vary-by-query="q">
       ...
   </cache>

   Caches the rendered OUTPUT of its child content in an in-memory store
   (IMemoryCache) keyed by the combination of vary-by values.
   The HTML between the tags is computed ONCE per unique cache key, then
   served from memory until the expiry.

   Attribute             | Type          | Description
   ----------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------------
   enabled               | bool          | true (default) / false to disable caching
   expires-on            | DateTimeOffset| absolute expiry date/time
   expires-after         | TimeSpan      | relative TTL from first render
   expires-sliding       | TimeSpan      | TTL resets on each cache hit
   vary-by-header        | string (csv)  | separate cache per User-Agent, Accept, etc.
   vary-by-query         | string (csv)  | separate cache per query-string key
   vary-by-route         | string (csv)  | separate cache per route value
   vary-by-cookie        | string (csv)  | separate cache per cookie name
   vary-by-user          | bool          | separate cache per authenticated user
   vary-by               | string        | arbitrary cache discriminator expression
   priority              | CacheItemPriority | Low / Normal / High / NeverRemove

   IMPORTANT: The cache tag helper requires IDistributedCache or falls back to
   IMemoryCache.  AddControllersWithViews() registers IMemoryCache automatically.
   ============================================================ *@
<h4>5. Cache Tag Helper</h4>

@* Cache rendered content for 5 minutes, shared across all users *@
<cache expires-after="@TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5)">
    <p class="text-muted">
        Cached at: @DateTime.Now.ToString("HH:mm:ss")
        (this timestamp does not change until the cache expires)
    </p>
</cache>

@* Separate cache entry per authenticated user AND per ?q= query param *@
<cache expires-sliding="@TimeSpan.FromMinutes(10)"
       vary-by-user="true"
       vary-by-query="q">
    <p>User-specific cached content (varies by user and search query).</p>
</cache>

@* Absolute expiry — cache until a specific date/time *@
<cache expires-on="@new DateTimeOffset(DateTime.Today.AddDays(1))">
    <p>This content refreshes at midnight.</p>
</cache>
